# ChiChat — environment variable reference
#
# This file documents variable NAMES only. Never put real values here — this
# file is committed to git.
#
# IMPORTANT — current architecture: the frontend does NOT read the two
# VITE_SUPABASE_* variables below today (VITE_CALL_ENGINE is the one VITE_
# variable it does read). src/integrations/supabase/client.ts
# intentionally hardcodes the Supabase URL and anon/publishable key, with an
# explicit in-file comment explaining why (a platform-managed .env used to
# point at a different, non-owned Supabase project and would silently
# override this). The two VITE_* names below are listed purely as
# documentation of what a from-scratch environment would need if that
# hardcoding is ever revisited — creating a real .env with these today has
# no effect on the running app unless client.ts is deliberately changed to
# read from import.meta.env again.

# ── Public frontend configuration (safe to expose in the browser bundle) ──
# The Supabase URL and anon/publishable key are meant to be public — request
# authorization is enforced by Postgres RLS, not by keeping these secret.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Optional, read at build time (set in Vercel, then redeploy). Empty or any
# other value = Agora for new in-app calls; "twilio" = Twilio Video.
VITE_CALL_ENGINE=

# ── Administrative / inspection credential — NEVER used by the app itself ──
# A Supabase Management API Personal Access Token, used only for ad-hoc
# privileged inspection/administration of the live project (e.g. via
# scripts you run yourself). This is NOT read by any application code, must
# never carry a VITE_ prefix (that would ship it to every browser), and must
# never be committed. Treat any token placed here as sensitive — set it,
# use it, then remove it again rather than leaving it configured.
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ── Backend secrets — configured as Supabase Edge Function secrets, ──
# ── NEVER in this repo or any .env file. Listed here for reference only. ──
# Auto-injected by the Supabase platform (do not set manually):
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# Agora (in-app calls, default engine):
#   AGORA_APP_ID, AGORA_APP_CERTIFICATE
# Twilio (Video calling + Voice/PSTN):
#   TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY_SECRET,
#   TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN, TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER, TWILIO_TWIML_APP_SID
#   TWILIO_VOICE_TWIML_URL is OPTIONAL — the code falls back to the
#   request's own URL when unset; only needed if this function ever runs
#   behind a proxy that rewrites the path Twilio's signature was computed
#   against.
# Google OAuth (Contacts sync/create, and the separate Google sign-in
# probe in check-google-signup):
#   GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET
# Push notifications:
#   FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON
# Voice-to-text:
#   OPENAI_API_KEY; optional TRANSCRIBE_MODEL
# Transactional email and reports:
#   RESEND_API_KEY; optional REPORTS_TO, REPORTS_FROM
#
# Set/inspect these via Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> Edge
# Functions -> Secrets. See docs/SECRETS.md for exactly which function
# needs which secret.
